<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Paphlagonia</h1><p class="st-meta">400 BCE – 6 BCE (approx.) · capital Gangra</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Paphlagonia, a kingdom of the forested Black Sea hinterland, ruled by local dynasts under Persia and later a pawn of Pontus and Rome.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Paphlagonians lived between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-bithynia">Bithynia</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-pontus">Pontus</a>, along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> coast and the forested mountains behind it, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cankiri">Gangra</a> as an inland seat. By the early 4th century BCE they had kings, such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corylas">Corylas</a>, mentioned by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xenophon">Xenophon</a>, who were nominally subject to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The rulers commanded cavalry and controlled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timber">timber</a> and the coastal towns. Thys defied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/datames">Datames</a> captured him c. 380 BCE. Later kings, often called Pylaemenes, sought alliances with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> while <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-pontus">Pontus</a> pressed them.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mithridates-vi-of-pontus">Mithridates VI</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-pontus">Kingdom of Pontus</a> occupied Paphlagonia in the 2nd century BCE. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome's</a> victory it was divided among client rulers; when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deiotarus-philadelphus">Deiotarus Philadelphus</a> died in 6 BCE, his kingdom was annexed to Roman <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/galatia">Galatia</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 400 BCE – 6 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:51.74%;width:7.84%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>400 BCE – 6 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Gangra</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Corylas, Thys, Deiotarus Philadelphus</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Anatolian and Greek religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Paphlagonian, Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Paphlagonia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-203&amp;focus=kingdom-of-paphlagonia" aria-label="Kingdom of Paphlagonia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5504 727 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Paphlagonia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5824 983L6140 1251M5824 983L5879 982M5824 983L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6140 1251h0M5879 982h0M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5824 983h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5824 983h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Gangra. <a href="/atlas?year=-203&amp;focus=kingdom-of-paphlagonia">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

